---
/**
 * What this site records, and how to stop it.
 *
 * Written before the endpoints it describes exist, so it states what Task 9 and
 * spec 02 will send. The opt-out flag is read by whatever loads them, and the
 * flag works from the day the button does.
 */
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What emptystat.es records, and how to opt out."
>
  <article class="prose max-w-prose font-mono text-sm grid gap-4">
    <h1 class="text-lg font-bold">Privacy</h1>

    <p>
      Three things are recorded here. None of them identifies you, and all three
      can be switched off with the button at the foot of this page.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-bold">Page views</h2>
    <p>
      Plausible, which is cookieless and aggregate. It records that a page was
      viewed, not who viewed it, and sets nothing on your device.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-bold">Which gallery layout you pick</h2>
    <p>
      Choosing between the justified and square views sends that choice to an
      endpoint on this domain. It is first-party, so <strong>an ad blocker will
      not stop it</strong> — the button below will. The count is a total per
      layout with nothing attached to it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-bold">Search queries</h2>
    <p>
      Queries are stored so the gallery can be improved against what people look
      for. No identifier is stored beside them: the text, and nothing else.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-bold">Opting out</h2>
    <p>
      This is honoured automatically if your browser sends Do Not Track or Global
      Privacy Control. The button sets a flag on this device only, so it needs
      pressing once per browser.
    </p>

    <p>
      <button id="optout" class="btn btn-sm" type="button">Opt out</button>
      <span id="optout-state" class="ml-2 text-base-content/60"></span>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var KEY = "es:optout";
    var button = document.getElementById("optout");
    var label = document.getElementById("optout-state");

    // A browser signal counts as opting out and cannot be reversed from here,
    // since the reader already asked once at a level above this page.
    function signalled() {
      return (
        navigator.doNotTrack === "1" ||
        navigator.globalPrivacyControl === true
      );
    }

    function render() {
      if (signalled()) {
        label.textContent = "Opted out by your browser's setting.";
        button.disabled = true;
        return;
      }
      var out = localStorage.getItem(KEY) === "1";
      label.textContent = out ? "Opted out on this device." : "";
      button.textContent = out ? "Opt back in" : "Opt out";
    }

    button.addEventListener("click", function () {
      if (localStorage.getItem(KEY) === "1") localStorage.removeItem(KEY);
      else localStorage.setItem(KEY, "1");
      render();
    });

    render();
  })();
</script>
